---
// /work — the real page, to the owner's full copy (28 Aug), styled with
// 21st. Import #12 is ziegfiroyt's Before/After Image Slider (demo
// 19250): the clip-path reveal with a draggable grip divider and corner
// labels, hand-rolled to zero deps (pointer events + keyboard arrows),
// carrying both artefacts. Both befores are GENUINE owner captures —
// A1's old DJ site and A2's old WulfTek site, each cropped to the same
// 1880×930 frame as its after, homepage to homepage, per the copy's
// honesty rules. (The Wayback route was checked and REJECTED:
// wulftek.co.uk archives an unrelated London IT firm.)
// Gates in force: WULFTEK_CONSENT=false omits the strategy sections
// (their commercial story publishes only with their explicit nod); the
// Harry quote slot ships absent per Q1; the optional agricultural-page
// capture awaits an owner-supplied frame.
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import Header from "../components/Header.astro";
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";

const WULFTEK_CONSENT = false; // flip only on WulfTek's explicit agreement

const djBuilt = [
  "A twelve-page website, designed and written from scratch",
  "An interactive window and door configurator",
  "A filterable gallery of completed work",
  "A production planning tool — eight stages, drag-and-drop scheduling, automatic deadline breach detection",
];

const wtBuilt = [
  "A multi-page website, designed and written from scratch",
  "A dedicated agricultural remapping section",
  "A vehicle registration lookup, so a customer can find their own car before enquiring",
  "Service pages for ECU, economy and performance remapping",
];
---

<Base
  title="Work — Talon Insights"
  description="Two businesses, two sites that couldn’t belong to anyone else — David Jackson & Son and WulfTek Tuning, with honest before-and-afters of both."
  path="/work"
  schema={{
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "WebPage",
    "@id": "https://taloninsights.co.uk/work#page",
    url: "https://taloninsights.co.uk/work",
    name: "Work — Talon Insights",
    about: { "@id": "https://taloninsights.co.uk/#business" },
  }}
>
  <Header />
  <main class="wk">

    <!-- ---------------- HERO ---------------- -->
    <section class="wk-hero">
      <div class="wk-wrap">
        <p class="t-micro eyebrow">SELECTED WORK</p>
        <h1 class="wk-h1">Two businesses. Neither site could belong to anyone&nbsp;else.</h1>
        <p class="wk-lede">
          Both started the same way — <em>time on site, before anything was
          designed.</em> What follows is what I found, what it changed, and
          <strong>what got built.</strong>
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ---------------- 01 · DAVID JACKSON & SON ---------------- -->
    <section class="wk-case">
      <div class="wk-wrap">
        <p class="wk-meta t-mono">HERITAGE JOINERY<i>◆</i>TELFORD<i>◆</i>WEBSITE + INTERNAL TOOL + STRATEGY</p>

        <!-- A1 — the slider (import #12) -->
        <div
          class="wk-compare"
          role="slider"
          tabindex="0"
          aria-label="David Jackson & Son — drag to compare the site before and after the rebuild"
          aria-valuemin="0"
          aria-valuemax="100"
          aria-valuenow="50"
          data-compare
        >
          <img class="wk-after-img" src="/images/work-dj-after.webp" width="1880" height="930" alt="The David Jackson & Son homepage after the rebuild." />
          <div class="wk-before-clip">
            <img src="/images/work-dj-before.webp" width="1880" height="930" alt="The David Jackson & Son homepage before the rebuild." />
          </div>
          <div class="wk-divider" aria-hidden="true">
            <span class="wk-grip">
              <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round"><path d="M9 5v14M15 5v14" /></svg>
            </span>
          </div>
          <span class="wk-tag wk-tag-l" aria-hidden="true">BEFORE</span>
          <span class="wk-tag wk-tag-r" aria-hidden="true">AFTER</span>
        </div>
        <p class="wk-caption t-mono">DAVID JACKSON &amp; SON<i>◆</i>BEFORE / AFTER<i>◆</i>DRAG THE HANDLE</p>

        <div class="wk-story">
          <div class="wk-block">
            <h2 class="wk-h2">What I found</h2>
            <p>
              Harry’s workshop is not a joinery in the general sense. The work that comes
              out of it ends up in listed buildings — sash windows matched to a
              two-hundred-year-old original, doors made to a conservation officer’s
              satisfaction, staircases that have to look as though they were always there.
            </p>
            <p class="wk-land">The website said “joinery services”.</p>
            <p>
              That gap was the entire brief, and it wasn’t visible from the outside. It
              became obvious standing in the workshop watching a window being made — the
              amount of knowledge in a single component, none of which was anywhere on
              the&nbsp;site.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="wk-block">
            <h2 class="wk-h2">What it changed</h2>
            <p>
              If the difference is in the making, the site has to lead with the making.
              Not a gallery of finished jobs sitting under a services list, but the work
              itself, photographed in progress, with the heritage and conservation
              language a customer looking for that standard would actually search for.
            </p>
            <p>
              Two other things followed from being there rather than from being briefed.
              Customers kept asking what their windows would look like before committing —
              so a configurator, letting them build their own and see it. And production
              was being planned on paper and in people’s heads, which is a different
              problem entirely, but I was in there&nbsp;anyway.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <h2 class="wk-h2 wk-built-h">What got built</h2>
        <ul class="wk-built">
          {djBuilt.map((b) => <li><i aria-hidden="true">◆</i>{b}</li>)}
        </ul>

        {/* [SLOT — Harry's quote. Omitted entirely until the real line
            exists. Never paraphrase, never placeholder. (Q1)] */}

        <p class="wk-case-link"><a class="wk-link" href="/work/david-jackson-son">Read the full case study →</a></p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ---------------- 02 · WULFTEK TUNING ---------------- -->
    <section class="wk-case">
      <div class="wk-wrap">
        <p class="wk-meta t-mono">PERFORMANCE &amp; ECU REMAPPING<i>◆</i>TELFORD<i>◆</i>WEBSITE</p>

        <!-- A2 — same treatment, same frame -->
        <div
          class="wk-compare"
          role="slider"
          tabindex="0"
          aria-label="WulfTek Tuning — drag to compare the site before and after the rebuild"
          aria-valuemin="0"
          aria-valuemax="100"
          aria-valuenow="50"
          data-compare
        >
          <img class="wk-after-img" src="/images/work-wt-after.webp" width="1880" height="930" alt="The WulfTek Tuning homepage after the rebuild." loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
          <div class="wk-before-clip">
            <img src="/images/work-wt-before.webp" width="1880" height="930" alt="The WulfTek Tuning homepage before the rebuild." loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
          </div>
          <div class="wk-divider" aria-hidden="true">
            <span class="wk-grip">
              <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round"><path d="M9 5v14M15 5v14" /></svg>
            </span>
          </div>
          <span class="wk-tag wk-tag-l" aria-hidden="true">BEFORE</span>
          <span class="wk-tag wk-tag-r" aria-hidden="true">AFTER</span>
        </div>
        <p class="wk-caption t-mono">WULFTEK TUNING<i>◆</i>BEFORE / AFTER<i>◆</i>DRAG THE HANDLE</p>

        {/* [A2 second capture — the agricultural remapping page, captioned
            THE PAGE THAT CAME OUT OF A CONVERSATION — awaits an
            owner-supplied frame.] */}

        {WULFTEK_CONSENT && (
          <div class="wk-story">
            <div class="wk-block">
              <h2 class="wk-h2">What I found</h2>
              <p>
                During a Groundwork Visit, a conversation turned to something the website
                barely mentioned: he remaps tractors.
              </p>
              <p>
                There is farmland on every side of Telford. There is also almost nobody
                competing for the words. Meanwhile every tuning shop in the Midlands is
                fighting over “ECU remapping” — a term with real volume and no way in for
                a business this size.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="wk-block">
              <h2 class="wk-h2">What it changed</h2>
              <p>
                ECU and economy remapping stayed front and centre. They’re the core of the
                business and nothing was taken away.
              </p>
              <p>
                But agricultural remapping got its own ground and real prominence, because
                that was territory he could actually own. Not a paragraph on a services
                page — its own space, written in the language a farm manager would use,
                aimed at people within driving distance who didn’t know the service
                existed nearby.
              </p>
              <p>
                That’s the Word Survey: the phrases your customers already use, that your
                competitors haven’t noticed, found by turning up and listening.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        )}

        <h2 class="wk-h2 wk-built-h">What got built</h2>
        <ul class="wk-built">
          {wtBuilt.map((b) => <li><i aria-hidden="true">◆</i>{b}</li>)}
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ---------------- 03 · THE PATTERN ---------------- -->
    <section class="wk-pattern">
      <div class="wk-wrap">
        <h2 class="wk-h2c">Both jobs found something the brief wouldn’t&nbsp;have.</h2>
        <div class="wk-prose">
          <p>
            A form would not have told me that David Jackson’s work belongs in listed
            buildings, or that Harry’s customers wanted to see their windows before
            ordering. A questionnaire would not have surfaced&nbsp;tractors.
          </p>
          <p>
            Both of those came out of being in the room, more than once, after the polite
            part of the conversation was over. That’s not a nice extra on top of the
            design work. <strong>It is the design work</strong> — everything after it
            is&nbsp;execution.
          </p>
          <p class="wk-land">
            It’s also why I can’t tell you what your site should be until I’ve been to
            see&nbsp;you.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ---------------- 04 · HONEST ABOUT THE LIST ---------------- -->
    <section class="wk-honest">
      <div class="wk-wrap">
        <div class="wk-honest-panel">
          <h2 class="wk-h2c">Two clients. That’s the whole&nbsp;list.</h2>
          <div class="wk-prose wk-prose-onpanel">
            <p>
              Talon Insights is new, and I’d rather say that than pad this page with
              logos I’ve had tangential involvement&nbsp;with.
            </p>
            <p>
              What I’d say instead is: look at what those two sites do that a template
              can’t, and at how specific each one is to the business behind it. That’s
              the part that scales. The number of them is a matter of&nbsp;time.
            </p>
            <p>
              I’m currently taking a small number of projects at a founding rate — same
              scope, same standard, in exchange for a written case study and a&nbsp;review.
            </p>
          </div>
          <a class="wk-link" href="/founding-projects">How founding projects work →</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ---------------- CLOSE ---------------- -->
    <section class="wk-close">
      <div class="wk-wrap">
        <h2 class="wk-h2c">Your site would be the&nbsp;third.</h2>
        <p class="wk-close-body">
          Start with fifteen minutes on the phone. If it sounds like a fit, I’ll come to
          you — and you’ll have a written scope and a fixed price before you’ve
          spent&nbsp;anything.
        </p>
        <div class="wk-ctas">
          <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/booking">Book a visit</a>
          <a class="btn btn-ghost wk-ghost" href="tel:+447742082423">Or call 07742 082423</a>
        </div>
        <p class="t-mono wk-reply">REPLY WITHIN ONE WORKING DAY</p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Base>

<style>
